<p>In the latest development, Israeli and Lebanese envoys held their first direct official meeting since 1993 in Washington on April 14. U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio hosted more than two hours of talks, and afterward the U.S. said both sides agreed to direct negotiations. The diplomatic opening was a rare point of contact between two states still technically at war. Lebanese President Joseph Aoun said he hoped it would mark the beginning of an end to the suffering, while a joint statement backed by foreign ministers from 17 countries said direct negotiations could help lead to lasting security for both Lebanon and Israel. The talks unfolded as fighting continued. Israel struck southern Lebanon and areas south of Beirut, Hezbollah fired rockets toward northern Israel, and Israel said it had hit more than 200 Hezbollah targets in 24 hours. Lebanon’s health ministry said Israeli attacks had killed at least 2,124 people in six weeks of war, including 168 children and 88 health workers, while Israel said 13 soldiers and at least two civilians had been killed. Later on Wednesday, a senior Israeli official said Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s security cabinet would meet to discuss a possible Lebanon ceasefire, a sign that even amid active combat, diplomacy may still have a narrow path forward</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/phrjpsRQDlCHINGkSMorVICGArJMukWAn_BrsYDgSfgQDKdhFxXSwOM8rHYLCUGHa0G45GtMo034hxYNm3TQB2l0d3jjD_pkr9eXX-OIanEr' alt='US Secretary of State Marco Rubio speaks during a meeting with Lebanon’s Ambassador to the US Nada Hamadeh Moawad and Israeli Ambassador to the US Yechiel Leiter at the State Department in Washington, DC, on April 14, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Parallel mediation: Senior Hezbollah official Ibrahim al-Moussawi said efforts by Iran and other regional states could soon produce a ceasefire, suggesting regional diplomacy was moving in parallel with the Washington talks</li><li>Hezbollah stance: Hezbollah rejected the Washington channel. Lawmaker Hassan Fadlallah called negotiations with Israel wrong and said the talks would deepen Lebanon’s internal divisions</li><li>U.S. approach: The New York Times reported that Washington praised the talks as historic but did not call for a halt to Israeli strikes or an Israeli withdrawal from Lebanese territory</li><li>State constraints: Lebanese officials and outside observers said Beirut has limited capacity to confront Hezbollah, even as President Joseph Aoun accused the group of showing &#x27;no regard&#x27; for Lebanon’s interests or the lives of its people</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Lebanese government: Ambassador Nada Hamadeh Moawad said she stressed Lebanon’s territorial integrity and sovereignty and called for a ceasefire during the Washington meeting. (<a href='https://theweek.com/world-news/israel-lebanon-rare-talks-fighting-war'>The Week</a>)</li><li>Israeli government: Ambassador Yechiel Leiter said he and his Lebanese counterpart agreed that Hezbollah should be eradicated, reflecting Israel’s focus on the armed group rather than on an immediate halt in operations. (<a href='https://theweek.com/world-news/israel-lebanon-rare-talks-fighting-war'>The Week</a>)</li><li>Hezbollah: The group dismissed the direct talks as futile and said any arrangements reached there would not bind it, underscoring the gap between state diplomacy and the armed movement’s position. (<a href='https://theweek.com/world-news/israel-lebanon-rare-talks-fighting-war'>The Week</a>)</li><li>Lebanese public voices: Reactions inside Lebanon were mixed, with some people welcoming a possible path out of the war and others condemning direct engagement with Israel after decades without official meetings. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/15/what-people-in-lebanon-are-saying-about-talks-with-israel'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3350220/israeli-security-cabinet-discuss-possible-lebanon-ceasefire-senior-official'>Israeli security cabinet to discuss possible Lebanon ceasefire: senior official</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://theweek.com/world-news/israel-lebanon-rare-talks-fighting-war'>Israel and Lebanon hold rare talks as fighting rages</a> - theweek.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/15/what-people-in-lebanon-are-saying-about-talks-with-israel'>What people in Lebanon are saying about talks with Israel</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c87ww2z0z3zo'>Israel and Hezbollah continue attacks after Israel-Lebanon talks in US</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/israel-says-struck-over-200-hezbollah-targets-in-lebanon-in-24-hours-11361086#publisher=newsstand'>Israel Says Struck Over 200 Hezbollah Targets In Lebanon In 24 Hours</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/638434-lebanon-talks-key-issue/'>US-mediated talks between Israel and Lebanon unlikely to resolve key issues – scholar</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1991819/us-hosts-rare-direct-talks-between-lebanon-and-israel'>US hosts ‘rare’ direct talks between Lebanon and Israel</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/hezbollah-says-lebanons-talks-with-israel-widen-national-rift'>Israeli security cabinet to discuss possible Lebanon ceasefire, senior official says</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/15/world/asia/israel-lebanon-us-talks-trump.html'>U.S. Applies Little Pressure to Israel to Stop the Fighting in Lebanon</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/hezbollah-says-lebanons-talks-israel-widen-national-rift'>Hezbollah says Lebanon&#x27;s talks with Israel widen national rift</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-lebanon-agree-to-direct-negotiations-after-productive-talks-us/article70863576.ece'>Israel, Lebanon agree to direct negotiations after &#x27;productive&#x27; talks: U.S.</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>